0..74 Comment "// Law 4 of the single-substitution calculus, `sub(sub(b, p), single(a)) ="
75..150 Comment "// b`: weakening then substituting for the new variable is the identity. It"
151..230 Comment "// does not hold by computation — at a variable `b` the substitution is stuck"
231..308 Comment "// — and is proved by induction on `b`: `substSquare` takes it to the shift"
309..359 Comment "// by zero twice, and `substId` takes that to `b`."
361..437 Comment "// The naturals; the syntax; the congruences, the composites\' square and the"
438..463 Comment "// identity substitution."
